<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P sets 'AA' rating on Queensland Treasury's bond.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P sets 'AA' rating on Queensland Treasury's bond.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp said on Thursday it had assigned its &quot;AA&quot; rating to Queensland Treasury Corp's 10 billion yen of five percent dual-currency dollar/yen samurai bonds due on February 28, 2000.</p>
<p>The rating reflected that of the guarantor, the State of Queensland, S&amp;P said in a statement. The rating on the bonds was constrained by the &quot;AA&quot; foreign currency sovereign rating of the Commonwealth of Australia, it said.</p>
<p>The foreign currency rating outlook was positive, it said.</p>
</text>
